{
 "id": "cast-arm-bracket-a356",
 "brief": "A bracket that carries the elbow joint of a small robot arm, cast in A356-T6 aluminium in a two-part\ndie that opens along Z. Every wall needs at least 2 degrees of draft and nothing may undercut the\ndie. Keep it inside x = 0 to 120, y = -20 to 20, z = 0 to 30. It bolts to the shoulder with two M6\nbolts along Z at (x, y) = (12, -12) and (12, 12): 6.6 mm holes through the full 30 mm height, each\nin a 16 mm diameter boss. At the other end an 8 mm steel pin along Z runs through a 20 mm diameter\nboss at (x, y) = (105, 0), full height. The pin carries 1200 N along -Y (the arm's weight and\npayload) and, in a separate case, 400 N along +Z. Safety factor 2, as light as you can make it\nbut under 150 g.",
